From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CMakeLists: patch fetched deboost.context for riscv64

deboost.context (fetched via FetchContent, pinned at 259fc4103bad) already
ships riscv64 assembly for its fcontext stack-switching routines
(asm/{make,jump,ontop}_riscv64_sysv_elf_gas.S), but its own CMakeLists.txt's
UNIX arch dispatch only branches on `arm`/`aarch64`, then falls through to
a CMAKE_SIZEOF_VOID_P-based x86_64/i386 choice for everything else. On
riscv64 this silently selects the x86_64 .S files instead of the riscv64
ones that are already present but unreachable dead code.

Insert the missing `elseif (${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "riscv64")`
branch into the fetched CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent's own PATCH_COMMAND,
before FetchContent_MakeAvailable() processes it as a subdirectory. The
`[=[ ... ]=]` CMake bracket argument keeps the embedded `$`, `"` and `\n`
tokens completely literal, so they reach `sed` unevaluated and only get
interpreted as CMake syntax later, inside deboost.context's own
CMakeLists.txt, in the same way the surrounding arm/aarch64 branches are.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not filed yet; the underlying arch-dispatch bug belongs in septag/deboost.context, which this project vendors via FetchContent rather than owning]
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -82,7 +82,12 @@
 FetchContent_Declare(
   deboost_context
   GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/septag/deboost.context.git
-  GIT_HASH "259fc4103bad6bb484d5ff426ace56ac557107a4" EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)
+  GIT_HASH "259fc4103bad6bb484d5ff426ace56ac557107a4" EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL
+  # deboost.context ships riscv64 asm (asm/{make,jump,ontop}_riscv64_sysv_elf_gas.S) but
+  # its CMakeLists.txt's UNIX dispatch has no riscv64 branch and silently falls through
+  # to the x86_64 one; insert the missing branch before its own FetchContent_MakeAvailable
+  # runs the subdirectory's CMakeLists.txt.
+  PATCH_COMMAND sed -i [=[s/# PC (x86\/x64)/elseif (${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "riscv64")\n        set(CPU_ARCH "riscv64")\n        set(ASM_EXT "sysv_elf_gas.S")\n    # PC (x86\/x64)/]=] CMakeLists.txt)
 FetchContent_MakeAvailable(deboost_context)
 
 add_compile_definitions(
